{"name":"Ski Slope","hex":"#e1e5e3","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ski slope","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An artificial construction, mimicking a piste, down which people may ski in places with no snow or no mountains","A mountain slope used for skiing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ski_slope"}],"entries":[{"title":"Alpine skiing","blocks":[{"text":"Alpine skiing, or downhill skiing, is the pastime of sliding down snow-covered slopes on skis with fixed-heel bindings, unlike other types of skiing, which use skis with free-heel bindings. Whether for recreation or for sport, it is typically practiced at ski resorts, which provide such services as ski lifts, artificial snow making, snow grooming, restaurants, and ski patrol."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Alpine_skiing_pictogram.svg/330px-Alpine_skiing_pictogram.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alpine_skiing"},{"title":"Ski","blocks":[{"text":"Skis are runners that are designed to glide over snow. Skiers employ them in pairs, attached to ski boots with ski bindings, with either a free, lockable, or partially secured heel. For climbing slopes, ski skins can be affixed at the base of each ski to prevent them from sliding backwards. Originally used as a means of travel over snow, skis have become specialized for recreational and competitive alpine and cross-country skiing. Skis may also be attached to vehicles, such as aircraft or snowmobiles."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ski"},{"title":"Slope","blocks":[{"text":"In mathematics, the slope or gradient of a line is a number that describes the direction of the line on a plane."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Wiki_slope_in_2d.svg/330px-Wiki_slope_in_2d.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slope"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Rastkogel_ski_slope.jpg/500px-Rastkogel_ski_slope.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Rastkogel_ski_slope.jpg/1280px-Rastkogel_ski_slope.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Rastkogel_ski_slope.jpg/500px-Rastkogel_ski_slope.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Alpine ski slope in the Zillertal valley, Austria","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARastkogel_ski_slope.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Base_del_Cerro_Catedral_en_Bariloche._%28Patagonia_Argentina%29_01.JPG/500px-Base_del_Cerro_Catedral_en_Bariloche._%28Patagonia_Argentina%29_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Base_del_Cerro_Catedral_en_Bariloche._%28Patagonia_Argentina%29_01.JPG/1280px-Base_del_Cerro_Catedral_en_Bariloche._%28Patagonia_Argentina%29_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Base_del_Cerro_Catedral_en_Bariloche._%28Patagonia_Argentina%29_01.JPG/500px-Base_del_Cerro_Catedral_en_Bariloche._%28Patagonia_Argentina%29_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Alpine ski slopes in San Carlos de Bariloche (Argentina)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABase_del_Cerro_Catedral_en_Bariloche._(Patagonia_Argentina)_01.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/SkiCollection.jpg/500px-SkiCollection.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thu